% Siblings Act
%
% The Logical English twin of a Blawx encoding, written by the Blawx translator
% (InsurLE2/migration/blawx). Each rule is a rule of the Act as Blawx encodes it,
% in the words of Blawx's own sentence forms, citing its section; the project's
% tests are the scenarios, with Blawx's own answers as the expectations.
%
% Source: the Blawx project "Siblings Act" (siblings.yaml, 4 sections), an example of
%         Blawx v1.6.22-alpha (Lexpedite, MIT licence), commit 3de892f67854292b304c9a55c5e2cd2058d3d418.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a person* is a sibling of *a second person*.
    *a person* is a person.
    *a person* is a parent of *a second person*.
    *a person* is a ward of the state; scenario element.

the knowledge base siblings includes:

the text of the Siblings Act is at "sources/siblings.md".

the text of the Blawx project is at "sources/siblings.yaml".

% The Act, section by section.
rule section_1 with provenance the Siblings Act at section 1:
a person is a sibling of a second person if
    the second person is a person
    and the person is a person
    and a third person is a person
    and the third person is a parent of the second person
    and the third person is a parent of the person.

opg is a person, as stated in the Siblings Act at section 2.

rule section_2 with provenance the Siblings Act at section 2:
opg is a parent of a person if
    the person is a ward of the state.

